#!/bin/sh
# The OS slot running now, for the login screens: "A", or "B (on trial: a restart goes back to A)" when it was started
# by tryboot and isn't permanent yet. With "issue", writes the console's /etc/issue from its template with the slot.
set -eu

partition=$(sed -n 's/.*root=PARTUUID=[0-9a-fA-F]\{8\}-\([0-9]\{2\}\).*/\1/p' /proc/cmdline)
case "$partition" in
	02) slot=A ;;
	03) slot=B ;;
	*) slot=unknown ;;
esac
permanent=$(sed -n 's|^os_prefix=slot\([AB]\)/.*|\1|p' /boot/firmware/config.txt 2>/dev/null || true)
if [ "$slot" != unknown ] && [ -n "$permanent" ] && [ "$permanent" != "$slot" ]; then
	slot="$slot (on trial: a restart goes back to $permanent)"
fi

if [ "${1:-}" = issue ]; then
	sed "s|@SLOT@|${slot}|" /usr/share/applpi/issue > /etc/issue
else
	echo "$slot"
fi
